This plugin is an independent, unofficial tool. It applies publicly described
self-organization methods, with attribution:

  - SMART goals: George T. Doran, "There's a S.M.A.R.T. way to write
    management's goals and objectives", Management Review 70(11), 1981.
  - The urgent/important distinction is attributed to Dwight D. Eisenhower
    (1954 address); the time-management matrix was popularised by Stephen R.
    Covey in "The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People" (1989) and "First Things
    First" (1994, with A. Roger Merrill and Rebecca R. Merrill).
  - The ALPEN method and the 60:40 planning rule: Lothar J. Seiwert.

All credit for the methods belongs to their authors. This plugin does not
reproduce their texts; it provides original guidance over the publicly
described methods.

